schema: "0.3"
id: echo-of-manifestation-map-petrified-forest
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  text: >
    Top-down dungeon map of the Petrified Forest — Zone 4 of Echo of Manifestation, a survival horror
    roguelite. Dark fantasy game design document style, bird's-eye architectural floor plan.

    The map shows an outdoor subterranean forest of stone trees with these areas connected by root-maze
    shadow corridors:

    ENTRY (south): A cave mouth opening from Zone 3's threshold corridor. Stone root archway frames
    the entrance. Small resonance shrine on a petrified stump.

    STONE CANOPY THICKET — COMBAT (center-south): 20m x 20m dense grove of petrified trees drawn as
    dark circular trunks with branching canopy ceiling overhead (shown as overlapping arc patterns).
    Roots creating natural barriers and chokepoints drawn as sinuous lines across the floor. Three
    essence nodes: hollow trunk center, root cluster east, petrified bird nest overhead. Four shadow
    nodes: canopy branches, root hollows, behind bark formations, inside a split trunk. Root grasp
    hazard zones marked with tendril icons near stationary positions. PETRIFICATION ZONES marked as
    gray-bleed areas that spread outward — contact causes player's shadow to begin turning to stone.

    GROWTH RING LABYRINTH — PUZZLE (west): 16m x 16m. Concentric rings of a massive petrified stump
    form a circular maze. Each ring drawn with gaps at different angles. Inner rings shown smaller
    than outer rings in proper concentric perspective. One essence node at center of the stump. Three
    shadow nodes between ring gaps. Ring contraction hazard marked with inward arrows and a timer
    icon showing 30-second cycle.

    AMBER CACHE HOLLOW — LOOT (east): 14m x 12m. Hollow formed by three enormous petrified trunks
    growing together, drawn as three large circles merging. Amber deposits in walls marked as golden
    amber inclusions. A fallen trunk creates a bridge to an elevated loot platform. Four essence
    nodes: amber deposits (2), elevated platform, root hollow. One shadow node embedded in amber
    (breaks free when mined). Amber resin spray hazard marked near deposit locations. A TIME DILATION
    POCKET on the elevated platform hidden behind amber deposits.

    MYCELIUM NETWORK CHAMBER — SECRET (accessible beneath root arch in Stone Canopy Thicket): 10m x 16m
    underground chamber drawn with dashed border. Glowing mycelium patterns on every surface shown as
    interconnected luminescent lines. Two essence nodes at mycelium junction points. Two shadow nodes
    dormant within the network. Spore release hazard zones near incorrect activation nodes. A
    resonance-matched petrified flower key icon at the entrance.

    THE HEARTWOOD ARENA — BOSS (north): 22m x 22m massive circular clearing. The petrified heartwood
    of the forest's oldest tree at center, drawn as a colossal trunk cross-section with growth rings.
    Root tendrils radiate outward like a sunburst pattern. Four essence nodes at cardinal root tips.
    Six shadow nodes: embedded in root tendrils, inside heartwood cavity, canopy perimeter. Root surge
    hazard shown as wave patterns emanating from heartwood. A TIME DILATION POCKET inside the
    heartwood cavity accessible after boss phase 2. Boss marker: "HOLLOW KING" with a crown-on-empty-
    throne icon. Absence zones marked as void patches that temporarily erase equipped items.

    The petrification mechanic is shown as gray-bleed zones that grow throughout the zone — the
    player's shadow icon at the map legend shows progressive stone conversion. Standing water patches
    in some areas marked as additional slow hazards.

    Map legend: Amber diamond = Essence Node, Purple circle = Shadow Node, Golden bubble = Time
    Dilation Pocket, Dashed border = Secret Room, Skull icon = Boss, Gray bleed = Petrification Zone,
    Tendril icon = Root Grasp, Void patch = Absence Zone.

    Style: Architectural blueprint on dark charcoal/obsidian background. Room borders in petrified
    gray with warm amber accents at node positions. Trees rendered as dark circles with root networks.
    Moonlight effect shown as subtle silver highlights along the tops of elements. No movement, no
    organic growth — everything mineral and still. Professional game design document aesthetic with
    geological survey quality.
  negative: "bright colors, cartoon, anime, 3D rendered, photorealistic, green trees, living forest, leaves, bright lighting, cheerful, colorful, low detail"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1536
    aspect_ratio: "1:1"

tags: [map, zone-4, petrified-forest, top-down, dungeon-map, game-design-document, dark-fantasy, stone]
